WEBVTT

00:00:15.169 --> 00:00:22.200
I'll never be easily loved...

00:00:22.409 --> 00:00:29.406
Am I just too clumsy?

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:36.615
That girl who looks good in pink...

00:00:37.258 --> 00:00:43.356
Is that who you want?

00:00:44.031 --> 00:00:47.990
Is red not good enough?

00:00:48.102 --> 00:00:55.008
The rabbit with red eyes runs away.

00:00:55.109 --> 00:01:02.379
Even though I loved you so much...

00:01:02.483 --> 00:01:10.483
If I'm sad, I'm going to die.

00:01:10.658 --> 00:01:17.223
The rabbit that you like...

00:01:17.798 --> 00:01:24.670
...isn't on the moon.
It's just a rabbit...

00:01:38.986 --> 00:01:40.112
Maniji...

00:01:42.356 --> 00:01:43.585
Manji!

00:01:55.636 --> 00:01:57.365
Manji, take this.

00:01:57.805 --> 00:02:00.638
It's an antidote
| learned from my mother.

00:02:00.741 --> 00:02:03.472
It's made from
pipevine and forsythia.

00:02:03.577 --> 00:02:05.511
It's not going to work.

00:02:05.713 --> 00:02:09.081
We don't even know
what poison Shizuma used...

00:02:10.884 --> 00:02:12.875
Just take it, okay?

00:02:14.088 --> 00:02:16.182
Where do you think you're going?

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:18.281
I'm going to get a doctor.

00:02:18.392 --> 00:02:21.054
Wait! Don't go
wandering around alone!

00:02:21.528 --> 00:02:23.394
I'll be right back!

00:02:24.131 --> 00:02:25.257
Rin!

00:02:27.868 --> 00:02:28.878
Styx

00:02:28.902 --> 00:02:31.872
At Arima hot springs for the month.
No patients. - Kakushin, Town Doctor

00:02:32.673 --> 00:02:35.699
A doctor wouldn't
be any help, would he?

00:02:36.443 --> 00:02:37.569
That's right.

00:02:37.678 --> 00:02:40.170
Manji doesn't have a normal body.

00:02:40.781 --> 00:02:43.478
A doctor can't do anything for him.

00:02:43.584 --> 00:02:48.886
If there's anyone who could,
it'd be someone the same way.

00:02:49.356 --> 00:02:51.085
Like Shizuma Eiku...

00:02:52.526 --> 00:02:53.960
But he's our enemy.

00:02:54.061 --> 00:02:55.290
Young lady.

00:02:56.096 --> 00:02:58.087
| figured it was you.

00:02:58.198 --> 00:03:00.292
It's been a while.

00:03:00.401 --> 00:03:03.132
Do you remember me?

00:03:04.872 --> 00:03:08.035
What are you crying
about out here this late?

00:03:09.043 --> 00:03:11.137
Your light's just so bright...

00:03:14.081 --> 00:03:17.107
There's no way this is going to work.

00:03:25.726 --> 00:03:29.287
I'm aware of your situation.
Come to my hideout.

00:03:29.396 --> 00:03:31.558
I'll mix an antidote for you.

00:03:31.665 --> 00:03:32.791
All right.

00:03:33.233 --> 00:03:34.826
You're barefoot...

00:03:35.703 --> 00:03:39.333
I was in a hurry...
Guess it looks dumb...

00:03:42.309 --> 00:03:43.687
Thanks for the sandals.

00:03:43.711 --> 00:03:46.442
Thanks for the sandals.
Not at all. This way's easier for me.

00:03:47.247 --> 00:03:50.547
Now, let's hurry there
and then hurry back...

00:03:50.651 --> 00:03:53.643
...before ol' Kanji bites the dust.

00:03:54.621 --> 00:03:57.818
You call Manji Kanji?

00:03:58.358 --> 00:04:00.554
Oh, right, I sure do.

00:04:00.928 --> 00:04:02.896
Your laugh sounds different.

00:04:03.564 --> 00:04:06.124
Didn't it go, “Hyohohohoho”?

00:04:17.778 --> 00:04:19.212
Big Brother...

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:20.872
Machi.

00:04:22.349 --> 00:04:23.817
Don't die...

00:04:27.988 --> 00:04:29.478
Don't die.

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:31.221
Manji!

00:04:36.964 --> 00:04:41.197
Do you know why
Manji and I are immortal?

00:04:42.336 --> 00:04:44.236
| heard it from Manji.

00:04:44.338 --> 00:04:48.741
Yaobikuni put some bloodworms
called Kessenchu inside you.

00:04:54.848 --> 00:04:59.581
They are the Buddhist monks'
ultimate means of prolonging life.

00:05:00.154 --> 00:05:02.122
They can halt bleeding...

00:05:02.222 --> 00:05:07.626
...and act in the place of destroyed
tissue when their host is injured.

00:05:09.129 --> 00:05:11.461
My body and his...

00:05:11.565 --> 00:05:16.093
...are just barely held together
by the patchwork of these vermin.

00:05:21.308 --> 00:05:22.707
Bloodworm killer.

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:25.507
When I was wandering
western China long ago...

00:05:25.612 --> 00:05:28.582
...I happened to get
a hold of this poison.

00:05:32.753 --> 00:05:37.486
Its role is to undo the patches
made by the bloodworms.

00:05:38.725 --> 00:05:40.716
Then Manijiis...

00:05:48.669 --> 00:05:52.196
That medicine that
looked like boogers worked...

00:06:00.414 --> 00:06:03.577
| missed my chance to die again.

00:06:07.855 --> 00:06:09.414
You're late...

00:06:13.827 --> 00:06:16.922
I'll be waiting by
the outer moat in Yotsuya.

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:18.589
Shizuma Eiku.

00:06:20.334 --> 00:06:24.703
That idiot! This is
why I tried to warn her!

00:06:36.283 --> 00:06:39.719
U-Um, I left the letter there.

00:06:40.087 --> 00:06:41.680
Yeah, thanks.

00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:44.919
U-Um...

00:06:51.565 --> 00:06:53.033
Who's the baby?

00:06:53.133 --> 00:06:56.967
My grandchild.
My son and his wife died before me.

00:06:57.070 --> 00:06:59.539
I'm the only family he has...

00:07:00.474 --> 00:07:02.306
I'm so sorry, miss.

00:07:02.409 --> 00:07:06.403
He threatened to kill him,
so I had to do this...

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:09.012
You don't have to apologize.

00:07:09.116 --> 00:07:12.086
I'm sorry to get you
wrapped up in this mess.

00:07:13.086 --> 00:07:14.178
Miss...

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:18.925
I'm sorry, miss.

00:07:19.626 --> 00:07:20.616
Just wait.

00:07:20.961 --> 00:07:23.396
I'll go call for help.

00:07:30.871 --> 00:07:32.361
W-Wait a second!

00:07:32.472 --> 00:07:34.531
What are you trying to do?

00:07:35.175 --> 00:07:36.267
Stop!

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:56.295
What are you doing, killing them?

00:07:56.396 --> 00:07:59.422
Damn it, you're no samurai!

00:07:59.533 --> 00:08:01.524
Die, you piece of shit!

00:08:02.669 --> 00:08:07.038
What do you have to cry about?
They were complete strangers.

00:08:07.507 --> 00:08:09.134
It's not like that!

00:08:09.376 --> 00:08:11.811
Why does someone with no blade...

00:08:12.245 --> 00:08:14.771
Why did they have to be killed?

00:08:22.856 --> 00:08:24.847
If you want to know...

00:08:24.958 --> 00:08:27.086
...will tell you.

00:08:33.667 --> 00:08:38.127
Two hundred years ago, still
during the Warring States Period...

00:08:39.106 --> 00:08:42.098
...| served under
a military commander.

00:08:42.876 --> 00:08:47.905
My wife and friends all
lost their lives because of him.

00:08:49.883 --> 00:08:54.980
| was so devoted to him
that I made my body immortal.

00:08:56.189 --> 00:08:59.124
| killed at least
one thousand opponents in battle.

00:09:00.794 --> 00:09:05.391
But all that remained at
the end of those long battles...

00:09:05.499 --> 00:09:08.867
...was the Toyotomi clan's
conquest subjugating society...

00:09:08.969 --> 00:09:13.133
...and my lord's head rolling
around in his fallen castle.

00:09:14.241 --> 00:09:19.475
Now that Toyotomi has also
perished, a thought occurred to me.

00:09:20.981 --> 00:09:24.849
What exactly were the people
who died in that war?

00:09:25.752 --> 00:09:30.121
Only a handful get to win a war
and leave their mark on history.

00:09:30.223 --> 00:09:34.558
The losers, even the commanders,
are nothing more than vermin.

00:09:34.661 --> 00:09:37.289
And those who couldn't
become commanders...

00:09:37.397 --> 00:09:39.889
...were just pawns from birth.

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:45.498
Enemies. Allies.

00:09:45.605 --> 00:09:48.233
We're all the same in the end.

00:09:48.775 --> 00:09:50.436
You and I...

00:09:50.544 --> 00:09:55.311
All of us are born as bugs
and will die like bugs.

00:10:04.291 --> 00:10:05.383
Sip it.

00:10:06.093 --> 00:10:10.553
If fresh wounds come
in contact, the blood will mingle...

00:10:11.131 --> 00:10:14.157
...and in rare cases
the worms can be transmitted.

00:10:16.369 --> 00:10:19.862
Earn the right to be able
to say life is precious.

00:10:22.342 --> 00:10:24.310
| want you to gamble.

00:10:24.845 --> 00:10:27.871
Live endlessly
and witness endless death.

00:10:27.981 --> 00:10:29.380
Then in time...

00:10:29.483 --> 00:10:34.114
...you'll come to see that one woman's
death isn't worth a second glance.

00:10:34.788 --> 00:10:38.747
And if you're immortal,
carrying out your revenge...

00:10:38.859 --> 00:10:41.920
...will probably
become simplicity itself.

00:10:47.801 --> 00:10:48.859
Afraid?

00:11:12.192 --> 00:11:16.789
What are you crying over
in this cramped little shack?

00:11:20.367 --> 00:11:22.233
Let's play outside.

00:11:22.335 --> 00:11:25.100
The moonlight's just right for killing.

00:11:25.572 --> 00:11:27.301
Isn't it, Shizuma?

00:11:33.313 --> 00:11:34.090
Infinity.

00:11:34.114 --> 00:11:34.205
Infinity.

00:11:35.482 --> 00:11:36.210
Infinity.

00:11:40.954 --> 00:11:44.185
| never hoped for anything from you.

00:11:44.291 --> 00:11:48.194
If it was this easy to infect
others with the worms...

00:11:48.295 --> 00:11:51.230
...| never would have
lost a single one of them.

00:11:54.601 --> 00:11:58.560
| figured it out.
The only thing I ever needed...

00:11:58.672 --> 00:12:02.973
...was a person just like myself.

00:12:03.577 --> 00:12:08.071
No way am I gonna play
the part of your wife, dumb ass.

00:12:14.321 --> 00:12:17.621
You don't know how
to hold back, do you, man?

00:12:17.724 --> 00:12:19.488
Manji, outside...

00:12:19.593 --> 00:12:21.459
The old woman's done for.

00:12:22.095 --> 00:12:24.689
The kid's fine, so go.

00:12:27.767 --> 00:12:30.429
You scared of seeing
tons of blood even now?

00:12:31.271 --> 00:12:34.434
If you stay, you'll end up
seeing something worse.

00:12:36.443 --> 00:12:37.410
Go!

00:12:41.548 --> 00:12:43.141
How can you move?

00:12:44.451 --> 00:12:50.049
| diluted the bloodworm killer's effects,
but you shouldn't be mobile so soon.

00:12:50.423 --> 00:12:53.484
So it's called bloodworm killer, huh?

00:12:53.593 --> 00:12:56.961
That stuff sure did
wonders for my mood.

00:12:57.063 --> 00:12:59.760
| wanted to talk to you again.

00:13:00.033 --> 00:13:03.560
And I still want to know
how you recovered so well.

00:13:04.070 --> 00:13:06.562
Traditional Chinese
medicine, I guess.

00:13:08.174 --> 00:13:09.300
You knew.

00:13:10.110 --> 00:13:12.169
It was a coincidence.

00:13:12.279 --> 00:13:16.307
Well, at the time I didn't
mind dying like that.

00:13:19.219 --> 00:13:21.381
But I changed my mind.

00:13:21.621 --> 00:13:25.057
Dying wouldn't seem right
if it was you who killed me.

00:13:33.133 --> 00:13:35.158
| was impatient too.

00:13:35.268 --> 00:13:39.501
If we're both immortal, there has
to be a twist to this ending.

00:13:40.106 --> 00:13:42.302
This is payback for the poison.

00:13:42.409 --> 00:13:47.609
I'll make you taste a level of agony
no normal human could ever reach.

00:13:51.151 --> 00:13:53.017
I'm looking forward to that.

00:14:22.048 --> 00:14:23.174
I'm sorry.

00:14:23.616 --> 00:14:26.381
I'll dig a grave for you later.

00:14:27.654 --> 00:14:29.349
I'm truly sorry.

00:15:18.671 --> 00:15:20.571
This isn't swordplay.

00:15:21.307 --> 00:15:23.639
Not even a fight to the death.

00:15:24.177 --> 00:15:28.637
You'll have to do better than that.

00:15:29.115 --> 00:15:32.380
Same to you, asshole.

00:15:36.890 --> 00:15:43.125
How many times do I have to suffer
the pain of having my heart stabbed?

00:15:44.898 --> 00:15:50.598
In the end, the only thing I can
share with you is this suffering.

00:15:50.937 --> 00:15:52.132
Right, Shizuma?

00:15:53.139 --> 00:15:55.130
I'll ask you once more.

00:15:55.241 --> 00:15:58.142
You have no intention
of defeating Anotsu with me?

00:15:59.546 --> 00:16:02.015
| harbor no grudge against him.

00:16:02.482 --> 00:16:07.147
But whatever genius he may be,
he's limited by his own mortality.

00:16:07.887 --> 00:16:12.552
We're better qualified
to control the Itto-ryu than he is.

00:16:13.026 --> 00:16:14.892
What do you think, Rin?

00:16:16.296 --> 00:16:18.890
Of course not, and I agree.

00:16:19.599 --> 00:16:25.060
It seems a man has to stick
by what he says in today's world.

00:16:25.638 --> 00:16:26.696
Why?

00:16:26.806 --> 00:16:29.673
Why don't you try
to grasp what I say?

00:16:29.776 --> 00:16:32.905
We seem to come
from the same mold.

00:16:33.313 --> 00:16:35.213
Just like me...

00:16:35.682 --> 00:16:38.652
...it's in your nature
to enjoy killing people.

00:16:43.389 --> 00:16:46.188
Guys like us turn up sometimes.

00:16:46.759 --> 00:16:51.390
We only truly feel alive
when we see blood.

00:16:52.232 --> 00:16:55.133
It's nothing to be ashamed of.

00:16:56.503 --> 00:17:00.906
But you should give up
on trying to stand above others.

00:17:01.441 --> 00:17:06.607
There's one thing guys like us
do once we come into power.

00:17:08.681 --> 00:17:10.274
We massacre.

00:17:11.951 --> 00:17:14.215
Well, what do you know...

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:20.259
They call you the Hundred-man Slayer,
yet you're surprisingly sensible.

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:22.228
It's amazing.

00:17:22.562 --> 00:17:24.030
Hey, thanks.

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:26.130
I'm not praising you...

00:17:26.633 --> 00:17:30.399
| thought we'd be able
to understand each other better...

00:17:30.503 --> 00:17:32.232
Such a shame.

00:17:33.873 --> 00:17:36.274
Manji, watch out! That's...

00:17:36.376 --> 00:17:37.537
I know.

00:17:39.879 --> 00:17:45.079
If I can't win you over, you're
nothing but a threat to the Itto-ryu.

00:17:45.985 --> 00:17:50.946
Soon it will be dawn. From here on
you'll have to put your life on the line.

00:17:51.624 --> 00:17:53.649
Life on the line, huh?

00:17:54.327 --> 00:17:56.523
That's a very human condition.

00:18:45.445 --> 00:18:46.412
Shizuma!

00:18:49.148 --> 00:18:51.344
Please die already.

00:18:52.485 --> 00:18:56.854
You've lived 200 years, and if you
haven't stood above others once...

00:18:57.857 --> 00:19:00.588
...then you'll be
a bug till the very end.

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:05.327
Golden Wasps!

00:19:18.511 --> 00:19:20.479
I'll hack you apart, old man!

00:19:44.203 --> 00:19:45.295
Manji!

00:19:45.738 --> 00:19:48.400
You pushed too hard...
Are you okay?

00:19:49.542 --> 00:19:51.340
Keep your voice down.

00:19:51.444 --> 00:19:53.208
It's killin' my ears.

00:19:55.081 --> 00:19:56.344
Look...

00:19:56.449 --> 00:19:59.680
Look at these wonderful worms...

00:20:00.053 --> 00:20:04.547
Manji, this body's just like yours...

00:20:06.759 --> 00:20:11.128
I'll tell you one thing while I still live.

00:20:12.231 --> 00:20:17.328
If you want to find
Anotsu Kagehisa, go to Fukagawa.

00:20:18.337 --> 00:20:22.934
You might run
into him, if you're lucky.

00:20:23.743 --> 00:20:25.802
How do you know where he is?

00:20:28.881 --> 00:20:30.349
Wait, Shizuma.

00:20:30.983 --> 00:20:33.975
Answer one question
before you go to sleep.

00:20:34.087 --> 00:20:36.818
Why didn't you
dodge my final attack?

00:20:39.092 --> 00:20:40.457
Girl...

00:20:41.194 --> 00:20:45.256
What you said before was true.

00:20:46.532 --> 00:20:51.698
But I've become tired of living...

00:20:54.107 --> 00:20:55.404
...as a bug.

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:02.345
Don't worry.

00:21:03.349 --> 00:21:07.047
I'll look out for him until
some nice person shows up.

00:21:07.153 --> 00:21:08.177
Thank you.

00:21:11.557 --> 00:21:14.618
Why did you make
a grave for him too?

00:21:16.162 --> 00:21:20.429
To “pay my respects
for 200 years of life," I guess.

00:21:24.904 --> 00:21:29.933
You know, he told me
he'd make my body undying.

00:21:32.845 --> 00:21:35.644
| figured if I was immortal like you...

00:21:35.748 --> 00:21:39.651
...revenge and other
things would be easier to do.

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:44.684
But at the time, I was...

00:21:44.791 --> 00:21:47.192
...I guess, completely terrified.

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:53.230
Not getting to die...

00:21:53.766 --> 00:21:56.394
Having to live forever...

00:21:56.502 --> 00:21:58.800
Just what does that mean...

00:22:05.211 --> 00:22:06.406
Say, Manji?

00:22:07.847 --> 00:22:10.009
Dying without reaching your goal...

00:22:10.116 --> 00:22:14.110
...or living a long time and then
finding out you can't reach it.

00:22:14.220 --> 00:22:15.813
Which is worse?

00:22:20.459 --> 00:22:23.224
You wouldn't find that out till you die.

00:22:25.698 --> 00:22:31.603
Sadly, I awakened...

00:22:31.704 --> 00:22:39.543
Overflowing reality is just...

00:22:40.479 --> 00:22:45.542
...more of the empty lies.

00:22:49.589 --> 00:22:57.589
To be honest, I have
to get ready for the next one.

00:22:59.265 --> 00:23:05.329
The morning slides
in from the window.

00:23:05.638 --> 00:23:12.908
Regardless of what
I see, I remember.

00:23:13.012 --> 00:23:16.277
| remember...

00:23:16.382 --> 00:23:22.754
The unchanging wind always...

00:23:22.855 --> 00:23:28.885
...just said this as it passed by...

00:23:29.295 --> 00:23:37.295
"What's needed for
this endless journey?”

00:23:50.082 --> 00:23:52.881
Where should I go?

00:23:55.254 --> 00:23:56.619
Infinite Preview

00:24:08.200 --> 00:24:09.634
Pizzicato
